## Stack

- Java {{ java_version }} via a **Gradle toolchain** (downloaded automatically if missing)
- **Gradle 9** wrapper, Kotlin syntax (`build.gradle.kts`), versions in `gradle/libs.versions.toml`
- **Spotless** with palantir-java-format for formatting
- **Error Prone** + **NullAway** for static analysis; packages are `@NullMarked` (JSpecify)
- **JUnit 6** + **AssertJ** for tests
{%- if profile == "backend" %}
- **Spring Boot 4** (Web MVC, Actuator, JDBC, Flyway, Postgres); Testcontainers for integration tests; `compose.yaml` for local Postgres
{%- endif %}
- **prek** for git hooks (`.pre-commit-config.yaml`)

## Layout

- `src/main/java/{{ java_package_path }}/`: production code (`{{ java_package }}`)
- `src/test/java/{{ java_package_path }}/`: tests
{%- if profile == "backend" %}
- `src/main/resources/application.yaml`: configuration
- `src/main/resources/db/migration/`: Flyway migrations (`V<n>__description.sql`)
{%- endif %}

## Commands

Use `./gradlew` (macOS/Linux) or `gradlew.bat` (Windows).

```shell
./gradlew build                 # compile + Error Prone/NullAway + spotlessCheck + tests
./gradlew spotlessApply         # format
./gradlew test --tests '*GreeterTest'
{%- if profile == "simple" %}
./gradlew run --args="Ada"
{%- elif profile == "backend" %}
./gradlew bootRun               # starts compose.yaml Postgres automatically (needs Docker)
{%- endif %}
uvx prek run --all-files
```

Verification sequence: `./gradlew spotlessApply build`

## Conventions

- Declare dependencies in `gradle/libs.versions.toml` and reference them as `libs.*`; never hardcode versions in `build.gradle.kts`.
{%- if profile == "backend" %} Spring Boot manages most versions through its BOM; add catalog entries without a version for managed artifacts.{% endif %}
- Always use the wrapper; never a system `gradle` or Maven.
- Every package has a `package-info.java` with `@NullMarked`. Mark nullable values with `org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable` instead of suppressing NullAway.
- Do not silence Error Prone findings with `@SuppressWarnings` without a comment explaining why.
- Prefer records and immutable types; keep classes package-private unless they are API.
{%- if profile == "backend" %}
- Constructor injection only (no field `@Autowired` in production code). Keep controllers thin and put logic in services.
- Schema changes go in a new Flyway migration; never edit an applied one.
- Use `@WebMvcTest` slices for controllers and `@SpringBootTest` + Testcontainers for integration tests.
{%- endif %}

